  "brief": "GE Vernova is acquiring Trench Group for $9 billion, while Ares Capital is acquiring MidCap Financial in a $2.6 billion deal, and I Squared Capital is acquiring Orizon in an undisclosed deal.\n\nGE Vernova / Trench Group (Announced): GE Vernova to Acquire Trench Group. GE Vernova is acquiring Trench Group for $9 billion [1, 2, 3]. The deal was announced on October 28 [1, 2, 3]. No further information is available [1, 2, 3].\nTrian / Wendy's (Announced): Trian Offers to Buy Wendy's. Trian is offering to buy Wendy's for $1.4 billion [4, 5, 6]. The deal has not been accepted yet [4, 5, 6]. The outcome of the deal is uncertain [4, 5, 6].\nDoorDash / Instacart (Rumored): DoorDash and Instacart Deal Rumors. DoorDash is in talks to acquire Instacart in a potential $17 billion deal [8, 11, 12]. The deal talks are ahead of DoorDash's Nov. 4 earnings report [7, 14]. Sources say DoorDash is nearing a $17 billion acquisition of Instacart [10]. The acquisition is reportedly part of DoorDash's efforts to wind down its Caper Carts business [9].\nAres Capital / MidCap Financial (Announced): Ares Capital Buys MidCap Financial. Ares Capital is acquiring MidCap Financial in a $2.6 billion deal [15, 16, 17]. The deal has been announced [15, 16, 17].\nI Squared Capital / Orizon (Announced): I Squared Capital Acquires Orizon. I Squared Capital has agreed to acquire Orizon, a leading advanced manufacturing company [18, 19]. The deal was announced on October 28 [18, 19]. No further information is available at this time [18, 19].\nKyivstar / GigaCloud (Announced): Kyivstar Acquires GigaCloud. Kyivstar is acquiring cloud provider GigaCloud for nearly $50 million [20, 21]. The deal was announced on October 28 [20, 21]. The acquisition stage is currently announced [20, 21].\nAlchemy / Freeit (Announced): Alchemy Buys Freeit. Alchemy has acquired Austin-based Freeit [22]. This is Alchemy's third acquisition in 2026 [22].\nBarry Diller / MGM (Announced): Diller to Buy MGM. Barry Diller is buying MGM [23]. The deal was announced after a pullback of a takeover bid [23]. No further details are available [23].\n\nAlso worth knowing:\n- CCC Intelligent Solutions earnings on deck amid $6.1B buyout [24].\n- Franklin Electric to acquire Australian pump maker for $181M [25].\n- Chantilly cyber firm RedLattice gets more time to close $1.25B SPAC deal after shareholder exodus threat [26].",
